# Agent workflow

1. Read `AGENTS.md`. For phase work or safety/mutation changes also read
   `docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md` and the architecture status block in
   `docs/ARCHITECTURE_0_3_IMPLEMENTATION.md`.
2. Prefer the matching `.cursor/skills/**` for this task
   (`execute-current-phase`, `spell-sync-ci`, `select-and-run-tests`, etc.) —
   do not load every skill up front.
3. Implement **only** the current architecture phase (or the explicit fix scope).
4. Run focused pytest; run `python3 scripts/check_architecture.py --check` when
   boundaries change.
5. Commit tracked changes and verify clean trees before final full CI.
6. Verify `python3 scripts/check_ci_evidence.py` after final CI; snapshot only after
   evidence success.
7. Read `CI_SUMMARY` and `CI_LOG`; fix failures without asking the owner to grep logs.
8. Update tests, docs, contracts, and ADRs together with code changes.
9. Do not claim pass without command evidence.
10. Capture baseline Git state for all three workspace repositories at task start.
11. Final task state: `git stash list` must be empty. Do not hide unfinished work in
    persistent Git stash between phases; use a named local branch with a normal WIP
    commit instead.
12. On modifying tasks: finalize workspace snapshot per `docs/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT.md`
    § Workspace snapshot, then report.
13. Do not advance to the next phase without owner approval (`advance-current-phase`).
14. Do not push, tag, release, or publish without explicit owner request.

